@startuml
title RuleSphere - Communication Diagram\n02. Author, Validate and Sandbox | UC-05..09
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam objectBackgroundColor #EDF5FF
skinparam objectBorderColor #496477
skinparam ArrowColor #496477
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 60
object "author : DecisionAuthor" as User <<actor>>
object "api : ManagementAPI" as API <<boundary>>
object "auth : AuthorizationService" as Auth
object "draft : DecisionVersion" as Draft
object "validator : DecisionValidator" as Validator
object "sandbox : SandboxService" as Sandbox
object "executor : GraphExecutor" as Executor
User --> API : 1: create/edit(graph, schemas, pins)\n2: validate(revision)\n3 [optional]: sandbox(revision, input)
API --> Auth : 1.1 / 2.1 / 3.1: authorize action and scope
API --> Draft : 1.2 [authorized]: save draft revision
API --> Validator : 2.2 [authorized]: validate(revision)
Validator --> Draft : 2.2.1: read exact graph, schemas and references
Validator --> Validator : 2.2.2: check DAG, scope, contracts and compatibility
API --> Sandbox : 3.2 [authorized]: execute(revision, input)
Sandbox --> Validator : 3.2.1: validate current draft and test input
Sandbox --> Executor : 3.2.2 [valid]: execute fixed sandbox snapshot
API ..> User : 1.3: save result\n2.3: validation issues / breaking status\n3.3: simulation result / error and protected trace
note bottom of Draft
Approved/frozen versions are not edited in place.
Cycles and invalid references block publication.
Breaking changes contribute to risk classification.
end note
note bottom of Sandbox
Sandbox is optional and has no production effect.
Invalid draft/input prevents evaluation.
Node execution follows diagram 06.
end note
legend bottom
  Read numbered messages, not spatial position. Nested numbers identify calls.
  1, 2, 3 are separate user requests. Failed authorization ends that request.
  Routine returns omitted; ..> is a displayed reply; [condition] is a guard.
endlegend
@enduml
